      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While over-the-counter treatments like eye drops, vitamins, and herbal supplements might provide temporary relief, they're unlikely to address the underlying cause of your symptoms. Before trying any new remedies, consider reaching out to your primary care physician, as they can offer guidance on affordable options or refer you to a low-cost clinic. Some migraines with auras do go away on their own, but over-the-counter treatments may exacerbate conditions that worsen over time.",
